  "description": "Back Garden (Left Boundary) \r\nT1: Goat willow tree – Fell to ground level\r\nCurrent height 3m and spread 1m. \r\nReduce height 0m and spread to 0m. \r\n\r\nT2: Prunus tree – Reduce height by 1m, remove epicormic growth \r\nCurrent height 4m and spread 3m. \r\nReduce height to 3m and spread to 2m.  \r\n\r\nT3: Olive tree – Reduce height by 1m through selective thinning, reduce sides by 0.5m to balance, remove x1 low branch on left-hand side with bird feeder attached, remove major deadwood \r\nCurrent height 4m and spread 3m. \r\nReduce height to 3m and spread to 2m\r\n\r\n(Right Boundary) \r\nT4: Bay tree – Fell to ground level, grind out stump \r\nCurrent height 2m and spread 1m. \r\nReduce height to 0m and spread to 0m\r\n\r\nFront Garden (Right Boundary) \r\n[Roadside starting from corner of road] \r\n\r\nT5: Fig tree – Prune overhang back to boundary (roadside only) \r\nCurrent height 3m and spread 3m. \r\nReduce height to 3m and spread to 2m. \r\n \r\nT6: Holly tree – Fell and leave stump standing at 2m tall  \r\n\r\nThe tree is causing damage to the wall. The roots may be pushing through or undermining the structure, leading to cracks or displacement. A concrete lintel has already been installed, but despite this, movement and structural stress are still evident\r\n\r\nCurrent height 4m and spread 2m. \r\nReduce height to 1m and spread to 0m. \r\n\r\nReason for work \r\nGeneral tree maintenance \r\nMore light \r\nTrees in decline\r\nLift over road low trees\r\nMaintaining this tree in its current setting\r\nOverhanging footpath",
